      "timestamp": "2026-08-30T22:31:53.365247+00:00",
      "type": "understanding",
      "summary": "Agent explained goal and mechanics.",
      "understanding": {
        "goal_understanding": "Navigate the grid to complete each level by stepping onto every goal cell only when the carried piece\u2019s shape, color, and rotation exactly match that goal\u2019s required attributes. Once all goals in the level are completed, you advance; failing by running out of lives ends the game.",
        "mechanics_understanding": "Each move costs 1 stamina; when stamina reaches 0 you lose 1 life and stamina resets to max, and losing all lives ends the game. Movement is constrained by walls, and each turn provides a 'blocked_directions' list that must be obeyed (attempting a blocked direction wastes a turn/stamina). Stepping on modifier tiles updates the carried piece: shape tiles cycle shape IDs 0\u20135 (wrapping), color tiles cycle colors in order orange \u2192 blue \u2192 green \u2192 red \u2192 orange, and rotation tiles rotate 90\u00b0 clockwise (0\u00b0 \u2192 90\u00b0 \u2192 180\u00b0 \u2192 270\u00b0 \u2192 0\u00b0). A goal cell activates only when shape, color, and rotation all match simultaneously; stepping onto an activated goal completes it. Stamina-refill tiles restore stamina."
      }
    }
